; Zone sink.test (TEST-ONLY). Every name under sink.test has its MX at the mail-sink container,
; except the step 2.3 names below.
$ORIGIN sink.test.
$TTL 60
@       IN SOA  ns.sink.test. hostmaster.sink.test. ( 2026110301 3600 600 86400 60 )
@       IN NS   ns.sink.test.
@       IN MX   10 mx.sink.test.
*       IN MX   10 mx.sink.test.
ns      IN A    172.31.250.53
mx      IN A    172.31.250.25
; Step 2.3 (docs/plan/steps/05-routing.md §6): the gateway's own inbound MX (postfix on mailtest).
gw-mx   IN A    172.31.250.10
; Domains of other tenants of this gateway: <anything>.gwtenant.sink.test (any depth) has its MX
; at the gateway MX (cross-tenant and loop tests): the closest encloser of those names is
; `gwtenant`, so this wildcard wins over `*` above (verified with CoreDNS 1.11.3). The bare name
; gwtenant.sink.test itself is answered from `*` (MX mx.sink.test); never use it as a domain.
*.gwtenant IN MX 10 gw-mx.sink.test.
; relay-sink: a tenant destination server that relays back to the gateway MX (loop tests).
relay   IN A    172.31.250.29
